# nr-exthost-worker-document-methods: document.preview, document.previewPages, document.libreOfficeStatus and document.installLibreOffice in mixdog-exthost-worker

Not compiled: cargo was not run (the lead compiles the wave).

## native/core/Cargo.lock

Package mixdog-exthost-worker: add `mixdog-rt` to its (normal) dependencies (it was a dev-dependency only; the soffice probe's
child budget uses mixdog_rt::time::timeout). No new package. Cargo.toml of the crate (owned by this task, already edited) also
adds the `process` feature of tokio (already enabled for mixdog-exthost, so mixdog-workspace-hack needs no change; take what
hakari prints if it asks) and the test target `document_twin`.

## SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs)

No name to remove: this task registers worker methods, not a protocol service (the document/* service is mixdog-exthost's
DocumentService, which already sends these four calls to the pool).

## Route (native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose.rs, fn native_ext_methods) [added in review]

The routed pool sends every name in `native_ext_methods()` to the Rust worker. Until the document engine below is
registered, the Rust worker answers OFFICE_PREVIEW_UNAVAILABLE for every conversion and every page render and skips the
font provisioning after an install, while the script worker still does all of it. So the document.* methods stay with the
script worker, as image.* do. Replace `native_ext_methods` and its doc comment with:

    /// The methods the Rust worker answers. The image methods stay with the script worker until the image corpus passes whole
    /// (AVIF and HEIF have no decoder yet), the document methods until the office-pdf document engine is registered in the
    /// worker (nr-office-pdf-preview): the list decides the route, nothing else does.
    pub fn native_ext_methods() -> Vec<&'static str> {
        mixdog_exthost_worker::native_methods()
            .into_iter()
            .filter(|method| !method.starts_with("image.") && !method.starts_with("document."))
            .collect()
    }

The wiring of nr-office-pdf-preview, which registers the engine, removes the `&& !method.starts_with("document.")` term.

## Registration of the engine (the office-pdf track's preview task, nr-office-pdf-preview, which is not in the tree yet)

Review notes: `Extension` is a plain `fn(&mut Registry)`, so the engine is built inside it, not captured
(`|registry| document::register_with(registry, Arc::new(<engine>::new()))`). The font provisioner already exists in Rust in
mixdog-app-server-daemon (domain_seams/office_fonts.rs, `prepareOfficeFonts`); the engine's `prepare_fonts` must reach that
one (moved to a crate the worker can depend on), not a second copy.

`document.preview` of a convertible type and every `document.previewPages` need documentPreviewPdf / documentPreviewPages and the
font provisioner, none of which exists in Rust at this point. `register_document_methods` registers the four methods over an
engine that answers code OFFICE_PREVIEW_UNAVAILABLE and logs the reason once at error level (a PDF previews in place, and every
refusal is the same). When the office-pdf preview library lands, its adapter implements
`mixdog_exthost_worker::methods::document::DocumentEngine` (preview_pdf, preview_pages, prepare_fonts) and the build registers it
as an `Extension` (`|registry| document::register_with(registry, engine)`), which replaces the four registrations. At that point
`PREVIEW_FORMATS`/`preview_format` in methods/document.rs should be replaced by the library's documentPreviewFormat.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-exthost-worker/src/main_entry.rs (not owned here)

The test `the_names_come_from_the_registry_and_an_extension_adds_to_them` lists the served names and is already behind (it lacks
the pdf.* and media.pdf* names); it also needs `document.installLibreOffice`, `document.libreOfficeStatus`, `document.preview`,
`document.previewPages` in its sorted list.

